files:   DIR [-a] [-l] [dir|pattern]   LS
         (DIR APPS lists it; DIR *.PAS, DIR ?.TXT
         match here; * any run, ? any one;
         -a shows the hidden .names)
         CD [dir]      CD - comes home
         MKDIR dir     RMDIR dir
         RM name       RM -f name
         (RM moves it to /.TRASH -- it is not
         destroyed; RM -f is the one that really
         removes it.  DELETE -l lists the trash,
         DELETE -r name puts one back, DELETE -e
         empties it)
         TYPE name     XD name
         EDIT [name]   VI [name]
         (EDIT: arrows Home End PgUp PgDn, Ctrl-O
         or Ctrl-S saves, Ctrl-X leaves.
         VI: hjkl 0 $ gg G, i a I A o O, x dd,
         :w :q :q! :wq, Esc leaves insert;
         /SYSTEM/ETC/VI.RC runs at startup --
         copy VI.SAMPLE there)
         NVIM [name]   Neovim, on the Linux, set
         up for the machine: F9 :make, F10 :Run
         LOAD name [addr]
         SAVE name from.to
         RENAME old new   CP old new
         RUN [name.prg|addr]
         EXEC script  (a # line is a comment)
         SWAP command
         (runs it on a clean machine and gives this
         one back: *SWAP name from a BASIC leaves
         the program in memory untouched)
         a bare name runs name.prg, looked for in
         /SYSTEM/BIN, /APPS/NAME, /LANG/NAME and
         /HOME/PROJECTS/NAME, with its args;
         F12 > Shell can also let it run name.COM
         on CP/M A: (off by default)
monitor: MON or WOZ [line]  then:  addr  addr.addr
         addr:b b b  addrR  X leaves
         FILL from.to value
         COPY from.to dest   (memory, by DMA)
system:  INFO [-v]   TIME   HUSH   RESET
         MODE [0-2|5-7]
         (0 640x480, 1 640x240, 2 320x240;
          5 1440x1080, 6 720x540, 7 360x270)
         COLOR fg [bg] [!]
         PALETTE [LOAD name|SAVE name|RESET]
         (LOAD GREEN, AMBER, GREY, PEPTO, C64 from
         /SYSTEM/ETC/PALETTES)
         ECHO   CLS   BANNER
         CLG (clear the bitmap; *CLG in a BASIC)
         ALIAS [name [text]]
         (ALIAS lists; ALIAS LL DIR -l defines;
         ALIAS LL with nothing after it removes.
         Kept in RAM: define them in STARTUP.BAT)
         CAPSLOCK [ON|OFF]
         DUMP [note|ON|OFF]
         SETUP (measures this computer once and
         keeps the clock it holds)
         BENCH (25 s: the clocks, 60 fps, 0 gaps;
         /SYSTEM/LOG/BENCH-NN.TXT)
         BUG (asks you about a fault and writes the
         report to /SYSTEM/LOG/BUGREPORTS)
tongues: EHBASIC  MSBASIC  BBC  FORTH  LOGO  RX
         CPM [command] (CP/M 2.2 on the Z80;
         K: is this disk, P: Turbo Pascal,
         D: WordStar)
         PAS name / CC name (compile name.PAS or
         name.C here into name.prg)
         in a BASIC, *command is the shell's and
         *BYE comes back here; *VI edits the program
linux:   !command / ! (the Linux beneath)
         SSH [user@]host
network: a URL is a file name:
         TYPE http://host/file
         CP http://host/x.prg x.prg
         CD tnfs://host/dir  (also ftp:// sftp://)
         MOUNT url /MNT/NAME   UMOUNT /MNT/NAME
         TELNET host port (F12 hangs up)
host:    F12 the settings menu   Shift+F12 pause
         Super+PgUp resets   PrtSc a screenshot
         k4510-menu.cfg hides menu rows and locks
         ! and the Linux consoles
boot:    /STARTUP.BAT runs at power-on.  If it
         wedges the machine, turn it off in
         F12 > Shell, or start --no-startup.bat
the handbook, on this machine: BOOK
         (BOOK 3 is every command, a line each;
         BOOK SHELL the chapter about the shell)
